==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-hang out to dry.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|hang<,,hung> out to dry}}

# {{&lit|en|hang|out|dry}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic}} To [[abandon]] someone who is in [[need]] or in [[danger]], especially a colleague or one dependent.
#: {{syn|en|leave someone hanging}}
#* '''2008''', Joe Fiorito, "[https://web.archive.org/web/20081202175321/http://www.thestar.com/printArticle/310368 Our home-care system '''hangs families out to dry''']," ''Toronto Star'', 7 Mar. (retrieved 23 Aug. 2008),
#*: Without supplemental health insurance, we would have been '''hung out to dry'''.

====Usage notes====
* Often carries an element of betrayal of someone who might have expected protection or assistance.

